<%# "Continue with Google": only while sign-up is open and Google credentials exist. POST-only (OmniAuth refuses GET), full page load (Turbo would swallow the redirect to Google). The browser's timezone goes on the form's query string: OmniAuth keeps the authorize request's query for the callback (omniauth.params), where a new account is stamped with it. The versions of the Terms and the Privacy Policy this page is showing ride there the same way, so a button drawn before a wording change cannot record an agreement to the new text (OmniauthCallbacksController#register). %>
<% if Registrations.google_enabled? %>
  <%= button_to user_google_oauth2_omniauth_authorize_path(LegalDocuments.version_fields), method: :post, form: { id: 'google_sign_in_form', data: { turbo: false } }, form_class: 'w-full', class: 'btn btn-outline w-full text-base normal-case gap-3' do %>
    <%= svg_icon('brand_google', class: 'w-5 h-5 shrink-0') %>
    <span><%= t('continue_with_google') %></span>
  <% end %>
  <set-timezone data-form-id="google_sign_in_form"></set-timezone>
<% end %>
